---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RetailDemo from '../components/RetailDemo.astro';
import data from '../data/retail.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const passed = data.meta.realism.filter((r) => r.pass).length;
---
<Layout title="Demo" description="One grocery basket, three domains: a supermarket in Bengaluru, its warehouse and its milk route, in a synthetic, seeded world." image="og/demo.png" wide>
  <div class="demo-page">
    <h1>One grocery basket, three domains</h1>
    <p class="lede">One supermarket in Bengaluru, the warehouse that supplies it and the dairy route that delivers its milk, through June 2026. Every number comes from a synthetic world built in the Domain Explorer project, seeded so every reader sees the same month.</p>

    <RetailDemo />

    <section id="logistics" class="demo upcoming" aria-labelledby="logistics-title">
      <h2 id="logistics-title">Logistics: the movement</h2>
      <p>On 22 June the warehouse truck makes its 06:00 slot. One pallet line is labelled 5 kg and holds 1 kg packs, and the store books what the shipping notice says. The retail view above already shows what happens next. This scenario opens with the logistics post.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}logistics/`}>Read the logistics outline</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="payments" class="demo upcoming" aria-labelledby="payments-title">
      <h2 id="payments-title">Payments: the money</h2>
      <p>The same store takes most of its bills over UPI. When a payment times out at the till, the customer can be debited while the shop sees a failure. This scenario opens with the payments post.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}payments/`}>Read the payments outline</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-world" aria-labelledby="world-title">
      <h2 id="world-title">About the world</h2>
      <p>The store reorders with a simple min/max rule on its own book stock, refills shelves twice a day, receives pallets by scanning their labels against the shipping notice, and counts everything at the start and end of the month. Customers, accidents and trucks are random but seeded. Two incidents are scripted on top, and the answer key lists them.</p>
      <p>{passed} of {data.meta.realism.length} realism checks pass. The world's out-of-stock rate, where out-of-stocks start, and how often stock records are wrong are compared with published studies; anything without a source is labelled as an assumption.</p>
      <details>
        <summary>See the checks</summary>
        <ul class="checks">
          {data.meta.realism.map((r) => (
            <li><strong>{r.pass ? 'Pass' : 'Fail'}:</strong> {r.check}. <span class="muted">{r.detail}. Source: {r.source}.</span></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </details>
      <p class="muted">Generated by <code>synthetic-data/india_grocery</code> in Domain Explorer at commit <code>{data.meta.commit}</code>, seed {data.meta.seed}.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
